course: dictionary
lesson: 306
title: Analyst: a person who studies information
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: An analyst is a person whose job is to study information closely, to understand it or to find problems. Think of a detective who looks at clues, except an analyst looks at numbers, facts or results.
explain: Analysts work in many fields. A data analyst studies numbers for a company, and a sports analyst studies games and players to explain why a team won or lost. The words around analyst tell you the field: «football analysts» study football, and «weather analysts» study the weather.
explain: The example says, «Many analysts expected Kyiv to fall within days in 2022; President Zelensky stayed in the capital and Ukrainian forces stopped the attack north of the city.» The analysts judged the situation from the information they had, and their expectation did not come true. An analyst's view is a careful judgement, not a guarantee.
fact: An analyst is a person who studies information closely to understand it or find problems.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «data analyst» and «financial analyst».
fact: «Analysts» is the plural, so one analyst means one person and «analysts» means more than one.
fact: In the US, analyst can also mean a psychoanalyst, a kind of therapist.
fact: Context clues help: words like «football» or «weather» before analyst tell you the subject the analyst studies.
exercise: What does an analyst do? | Teaches children to swim | Builds houses from bricks | *Studies information closely to understand it or find problems | Sells cars to customers
exercise: «Financial analyst» suggests a person who studies what? | Animals in the wild | Old castles | *Money and business information | Songs for the radio
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Many analysts expected Kyiv to fall within days» that means more than one analyst. | expected | Kyiv | within | *analysts
test: Which job would a sports analyst most likely do? | Repair bicycles | Paint pictures of horses | Bake bread for a café | *Explain why a team won by studying the game
test: Why does the sentence about Kyiv show that an analyst's view can be wrong? | Analysts always agree with each other | *The analysts expected Kyiv to fall, but it did not | Kyiv is too big to predict | Analysts never look at the news
exam: A friend says, «She is a data analyst.» What is the best guess for her job? | Driving a bus across the city | *Studying numbers and information for a company | Painting walls in a school | Baking cakes for a shop
